course: dictionary
lesson: 13221
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and «gaffer» is one of them. You do not need to guess blindly. The words around it show you which meaning fits, so ask yourself who is talking and where they are.
explain: «The gaffer told the team to train harder on Monday.» The team and the training are the clues. A gaffer here is the boss, such as a football manager. In «The gaffer on the film set checked every light», the clues are film set and lights, so the gaffer is the chief electrician.
explain: «An old gaffer sat by the gate, smoking his pipe.» Old and sitting by a gate tell you this gaffer is an old man from the countryside. Test it: does "an old boss sat by the gate" make sense? Probably not, so this is a different meaning.
fact: Gaffer is an informal word, so you will hear it more in everyday talk than in formal writing.
fact: In British English, «the gaffer» usually means the boss or the football manager.
fact: On a film set, the gaffer is the chief electrician who looks after the lights.
fact: «An old gaffer» can mean an old man, especially in the countryside.
fact: Phrases you may hear include «ask the gaffer», «the gaffer said» and «gaffer tape».
exercise: «The gaffer told the team to train harder on Monday.» What does gaffer mean here? | A sunny day at the beach | *The boss, such as a football manager | A pair of football boots
exercise: «The gaffer on the film set checked every light before the cameras rolled.» What job does the gaffer do? | *The chief electrician who looks after the lights | The actor who plays the hero | The person who writes the script
exercise: «An old gaffer sat by the gate, smoking his pipe.» Who is the gaffer here? | *An old man, especially in the countryside | A young football player | A film director
test: «Ask the gaffer if we can go home early.» Who is the best person to ask? | The dog next door | The moon | *The boss in charge
test: Which sentence uses gaffer to mean an old man? | *«An old gaffer leaned on the fence and waved.» | «The gaffer checked the lights on set.» | «The gaffer said we could start.»
exam: «The gaffer of the club said the new striker would start on Saturday.» Which clue shows that gaffer means the boss? | *The club and the striker, because a football club has a manager in charge | Gaffer means a lamp, so it is about light | The striker is a kind of gaffer | Saturday is the name of the gaffer
